lint_2.5.0_windows_arm64.zip","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/zip","state":"uploaded","size":7614881,"digest":"sha256:d446527b6fbe1247401f19baa540ff2e6489671616c9721bd9e7d7caa986d2f3","download_count":1,"created_at":"2026-11-05T17:59:09Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T17:59:10Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/jdx/jactionlint/releases/download/v2.5.0/jactionlint_2.5.0_windows_arm64.zip"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/jactionlint/releases/assets/714300882","id":714300882,"node_id":"RA_kwDOU73bVs4qk13S","name":"packslip.sigstore.json","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":21645,"digest":"sha256:a82748ede056314030fa429488763430023cd8511f1b86e42cf8fb364a860b52","download_count":361,"created_at":"2026-11-05T17:59:59Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T17:59:59Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/jdx/jactionlint/releases/download/v2.5.0/packslip.sigstore.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/jactionlint/tarball/v2.5.0","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/jactionlint/zipball/v2.5.0","body":"jactionlint 2.5.0 adds `jactionlint run`, which runs the jobs of a workflow on your machine inside an OS sandbox, without a container engine. It also adds the `unreachable-required-check` rule, fixes two `unpinned-images` issues, and accepts the `apm` Dependabot ecosystem.\n\n## Added\n\n### `jactionlint run`: run workflows locally\n\n`jactionlint run` lets you debug a `run:` script, an expression, a matrix or the `needs` wiring without pushing a commit. It shows what happened on your machine, not whether the workflow will pass on GitHub. Every skip or refusal is printed with its reason, and the [run guide](https://github.com/jdx/jactionlint/blob/main/docs/run.md) has a \"Differences from GitHub\" table. The workflow is first linted with the `correctness` profile, and the run stops on an error (`--no-lint` skips the lint). (#316, #317, #319, #320, #321, #322, #323, #324, @jdx)\n\n```sh\njactionlint run --list                    # jobs and matrix cells in dependency order, nothing runs\njactionlint run ci -j test                # run job `test` of .github/workflows/ci.yml and the jobs it needs\njactionlint run ci --dry-run              # the steps with ${{ }} replaced, nothing runs\njactionlint run ci -e pull_request --secret TOKEN=abc --var REGION=eu\njactionlint run --check-sandbox           # what this machine can enforce\n```\n\n- **Plan view.** `--list` (`--json` for JSON) groups jobs into stages and expands matrices the way the runner does: `exclude`, then `include`. It evaluates `name:`, `runs-on:` and job `if:` expressions that it can, and marks each one `if is true` or `if is false`. The `github` context comes from git, `-i NAME=VALUE` sets `workflow_dispatch` inputs, and `--event-file` supplies `github.event`. A matrix built from `needs` outputs shows as \"known at run time\".\n- **Steps and jobs.** Supports `run:` steps with `shell`, `working-directory`, `defaults.run`, layered `env`, `timeout-minutes` and `continue-on-error`. Also supported: step and job outputs, `needs.*.result`, matrices with `fail-fast`, background and `parallel:` steps, the `GITHUB_ENV`/`PATH`/`OUTPUT`/`STATE`/`STEP_SUMMARY` file commands and workflow commands. Values from `--secret` and `::add-mask::` show as `***` in all output. Jobs whose `runs-on` names a different OS are skipped. Ctrl-C cancels the steps, and steps with `if: always()` still run.\n- **Actions and reusable workflows.** Runs local, composite and JavaScript actions (with `pre`/`post`) and local or remote reusable workflows. If no Node.js on `PATH` has the right major version, jactionlint downloads it and checks it against the release's `SHASUMS256.txt`. **Remote actions and reusable workflows must be pinned to a commit SHA.** Use `--trust-actions` to resolve a tag or branch and print the commit it picked. `actions/checkout`, `upload-artifact` and `download-artifact` are replaced with local versions. Use `--no-shim ACTION` to run the real action.\n- **Local actions cache.** A cache service on `127.0.0.1` works with unmodified `actions/cache`, `setup-*`, `jdx/mise-action` and other actions built on `@actions/cache`, so a second run restores instead of downloading again. Caches are scoped to the ref and fall back to the default branch. Entries expire after 7 days, and the store has a 10 GB LRU limit (`--cache-size`). Related options: `--cache=read-only|off`, `--no-cache`, `--cache-dir`. Manage the store with `jactionlint cache ls|rm|prune|path`.\n- **Network modes.** `--net=open` is the default. `--net=none` blocks internet sockets. `--net=proxy` allows only a proxy that lets through GitHub and the common package registries. It needs Landlock ABI 4, which is Linux 6.7 or later. `--allow-net HOST,...` adds hosts, and `--learn` prints the hosts your steps contacted.\n- **Containers (optional).** `container:` jobs, `services:` and Docker actions run through `docker` or `podman` (`--container-engine`). By default all capabilities are dropped except nine, and `no-new-privileges` is set. jactionlint never runs privileged containers or mounts the host home or Docker socket. Images must be pinned by digest unless you pass `--trust-images`. `options:` is checked against an allow list: `--privileged`, `--cap-add`, `-v`, `--network host` and similar options are refused unless you pass `--unsafe-container-options`. Use `--container` to run Linux matrix cells in a digest-pinned `ubuntu` image, for example from a Mac. If no engine is installed, or you pass `--no-containers`, only the jobs and steps that need a container are skipped.\n- **Parallel runs.** `--parallel N` runs matrix cells and independent jobs at the same time. It respects `needs` and `max-parallel`, and prints each job's output in one block.\n- **Explanations.** Messages that end with `(jactionlint run --explain ID)` have a longer explanation. `jactionlint run --explain list` lists all of them.\n\n**Isolation and platform support:** Each step runs with a filtered environment, a throwaway home, and a per-job copy of the workspace. Your checkout and real home cannot be read or written. Use `--in-place` to work in your checkout, `--allow-read`/`--allow-write DIR` to open more paths, and `--sandbox=off` to turn the sandbox off. If the sandbox can't be applied, the step does not run.\n- **Linux:** Landlock and seccomp-bpf, Linux 5.13 or later.\n- **macOS:** Seatbelt through `sandbox-exec`. This backend is new and has had much less use than the Linux one.\n- **Windows:** steps are refused. Use WSL2.\n\n### New rule: `unreachable-required-check`\n\nThe new `unreachable-required-check` rule reports a required check that no workflow will report for a change. GitHub waits forever for such a check, and the pull request cannot merge. Common causes are a missing `merge_group` trigger, a `branches` filter that leaves out the protected branch, and a `paths` filter that skips a README-only change. (#331, @mariusvniekerk)\n\nThe rule turns on in every profile when `required-checks` is in the config file:\n\n```yaml\nrequired-checks:\n  - name: CI gate\n    events: [pull_request, merge_group]   # default: [pull_request]\n    branches: [main]                      # optional, literal names\n```\n\nIt reads every workflow in `.github/workflows`, so it doesn't report GitHub's workaround of a second workflow with the opposite `paths` filter. Each finding is placed where the fix goes: the config declaration (with a \"did you mean\" suggestion), `on:`, or the filter. When the answer depends on something the rule doesn't evaluate, it reports at level `info` and gives the reason. It does not read branch protection or rulesets from GitHub, so keep the list in sync with your repository settings. To turn the rule off, set `rules: {unreachable-required-check: off}`.\n\n## Fixed\n\n- **`unpinned-images`** now treats images built by drop-in forks of `docker/build-push-action` as local, the same as the original: `useblacksmith/build-push-action`, `depot/build-push-action` and `warpbuilds/build-push-action`. A later `docker run` of the image's tag is no longer reported. Other actions that take a `tags:` input are still reported. (#328, @jdx, @tedserbinski)\n- **`unpinned-images`** now only treats an image as local when the same job builds, tags or loads it. Each job runs on its own runner, so `docker run app:ci` in a job that doesn't build `app:ci` pulls the image from the registry. That use is now reported. Previously, a build anywhere in the workflow hid the finding in every job. (#329, @jdx, @tedserbinski)\n- **`dependabot-syntax`** accepts `package-ecosystem: apm` (Agent Package Manager), which GitHub added on November 3, 2026. (#333, @frottke)\n\n## New Contributors\n\n* @mariusvniekerk made their first contribution in #331\n* @frottke made their first contribution in #333\n* @tedserbinski made their first contribution in 4d0fcf65 (#328)\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/jdx/jactionlint/compare/v2.4.0...v2.5.0\n\n## 💚 Sponsor jactionlint\n\njactionlint is a fork of [rhysd/actionlint](https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint), maintained by [@jdx](https://github.com/jdx), an open source developer at [**entire.io**](https://entire.io/), the title sponsor of his open source work.\n\nIf jactionlint has a place in your development workflow, please consider becoming an [individual or company sponsor](https://jdx.dev/sponsors.html). Your support funds ongoing development and helps keep jactionlint fast, free, and independent.\n","mentions_count":4}